TITLE:: RLChord
summary:: A chord: a root and a type in a chord space
categories:: Libraries>reLation
related:: Classes/RLChordSpace, Classes/RLChordContext, Classes/RLTransform, Classes/RLWalk, Guides/reLation

DESCRIPTION::
A chord of a link::Classes/RLChordSpace::. Its strong::root:: is a pitch class of the space's system (an Integer in link::Classes/RLEDO::, an Array of exponents in link::Classes/RLJust::), its strong::type:: one of the space's names. Its tones follow from the type's pattern, root first.

A chord is a value: two chords with the same root and type in equal spaces are equal, hash alike, and can be the keys of a Dictionary or the members of a Set. It carries no octave and no voicing: a voicing is an Array of pitches (link::Classes/RLVoiceLeading::).

code::
~space = RLChordSpace.triads(RLEDO(12));
~c = ~space.major(0);
~c.pcs;                              // [0, 4, 7]
~c.name;                             // C major
~c == ~space.chord(0, \major);       // true
~c.commonPcs(~space.minor(4));       // [4, 7]: what C major shares with E minor
RLChordSpace.triads(RLJust([3, 5])).minor([-1, 1]).name;   // 5/3 minor
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Usually made by the space: code::space.chord(root, type)::, code::space.major(root)::.
argument:: space
argument:: root
A pitch class, reduced to the system's own form (14 becomes 2 in 12 steps).
argument:: type
A name of the space; an unknown one is an Error.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: space
METHOD:: root
METHOD:: type

METHOD:: system
The space's pitch system.

METHOD:: typeIndex
The index of its type in the space.

METHOD:: pcs
The pitch classes of its tones, in the order of the type's pattern (root, third, fifth).

METHOD:: hasPcs
Whether these pitch classes, in any order, are its tones.

METHOD:: commonPcs
The tones shared with another chord.

METHOD:: name
code::"C major"::, code::"7 minor":: in a division without note names, code::"5/3 minor":: on the lattice. A chord prints as its name.
